  "application_type_full": "Householder planning & listed building consent",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\nPP-14967771v1 Location Plan dated 28 May 2026; 1328 EX_100 P1 Existing Location Plan dated January 2026; 1328 EX_103 P1 Existing First Floor Plan dated February 2023; 1328 EX_104 P1 Existing Roof Plan dated February 2023; 1328 108 P1 Proposed Roof Plan dated January 2026; 1328 108 P1 Proposed Roof Plan dated January 2026; 1328 545 P1 Roof Valley Section Detail dated January 2026; Heritage, Design & Access Statement Rev P1 dated May 2026; CISBE TM 59 Overheating Report Rev 03 dated 16/06/2026; 1328 546 P1 Proposed Master Bedroom (RF07) Ceiling Vent Detail dated January 2026; 15140/1 Plant Noise Impact Assessment dated 11/06/2026.\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application. \r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policy D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The external noise level emitted from plant, machinery or equipment at the development with specified noise mitigation hereby approved shall be lower than the typical existing background noise level by at least 10dBA, by 15dBA where the source is tonal, as assessed according to BS4142:2014 at the nearest and/or most affected noise sensitive premises, with machinery operating at maximum capacity and thereafter be permanently retained.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the amenity of occupiers of the development site/ surrounding premises is not adversely affected by noise from mechanical installations/ equipment in accordance with the requirements of policies A1 and A4 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to use, machinery, plant or equipment at the development shall be mounted with proprietary anti-vibration isolators and fan motors shall be vibration isolated from the casing and adequately silenced and maintained as such. \r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the amenity of occupiers of the development site and surrounding premises is not adversely affected by vibration in accordance with the requirements of policies A1 and A4 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to use, evidence shall be submitted and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, demonstrating that measures to adapt to climate change have been implemented and that overheating risk has been managed. It needs to demonstrate that the development has reduced cooling demand as far as possible and that the cooling hierarchy has been followed and any feasible measures implemented. The measures to be implemented should at a minimum include internal blinds and external awnings.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that all development reduce the impact of urban and dwelling overheating, including application of the cooling hierarchy in accordance with policy CC2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan.\r\n"
  ],
